{
  "id": 1004,
  "name": "Branch on an HTTP status code",
  "description": "## What it does\n\nCalls an endpoint, then uses an **If** node to branch on `statusCode`. The healthy branch does nothing; the unhealthy branch is where you would add a Slack message, an email, or a ticket.\n\n## Setup\n\n1. Run the workflow manually. The URL points at `https://httpbin.org/status/200`, so the healthy branch runs by default.\n2. Change the URL to `https://httpbin.org/status/500` and run it again to exercise the unhealthy branch.\n3. Replace the example URL and NoOp nodes with your endpoint and desired actions.\n\n## Notes\n\nThe HTTP Request node returns the full response and ignores HTTP error statuses, so the status code stays available to the If node instead of throwing first.",
